provider: ollama-cloud (glm-5.3)
request: Rename the `watched` field of watchlist items to `seen` everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> movie, watchlist-store, watchlist, search, movie-detail, app  (Pure data-field rename: the watchlist-item state field `watched` becomes `seen`. The `movie` unit declares the new interface shape (Movie + WatchItem); every consumer (watchlist-store and the components that render or read items) must switch all reads/writes of that field — in TypeScript and in templates — while keeping every other identifier (toggleWatched, watchedCount, progress, UI strings) unchanged. Acceptance tests pin the new field name on stored items and through the watchlist component.)
round 1: owners movie=ok watchlist-store=ok watchlist=rejected search=ok movie-detail=ok app=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist  (The rename landed in every unit except watchlist, whose whole submission was rejected because it edited an existing test. That edit is exactly what the request requires — the test reads `items[0].watched`, a field that no longer exists on `WatchItem` — so I approve it and re-instruct the watchlist owner to redo the full sweep. The oracle errors (spec line 66 and the template of component Watchlist) are all confined to that unit.)
round 2: owners watchlist=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 3: plan -> watchlist  (tsc is green so the watched→seen rename is complete; the only failures are test infrastructure: my watchlist acceptance test created the component without router providers (NG0201 from routerLink), which I fix by replacing it with a provideRouter-based version, and the watchlist spec's axe test timed out at 5000ms, which the watchlist owner must stabilize (timeout-only change pre-approved if the component is sound).)
round 3: owners watchlist=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 4: accept  (The rename is complete: the Movie and WatchItem interfaces now expose `seen: boolean` (no `watched` field anywhere), and every consumer that reads or writes the item's watched state (watchlist-store's add/toggleWatched/watchedCount and persistence, the watchlist component's bindings) was updated accordingly. search, movie-detail and app were verified to have no references to the field. The oracle is green (tsc exit 0, 42/42 vitest tests passing), and the acceptance tests pin the new behaviour: items are created with `seen: false`, `toggleWatched` flips `seen`, stored items carry no `watched` key, and the watchlist component renders and toggles items through `seen`. Per the request, only the item field was renamed; method names like `toggleWatched`/`watchedCount` and user-facing strings were deliberately left unchanged. The request is satisfied.)

